### Output Format
Respond with XML inside a `<synthesis>` root element (no other text).

Required elements and their attributes:
- `<claims>` containing `<claim id="C{n}" agreement="..." corroboration_count="{n}">` elements, each with `<text>`, `<sources>` (with `<source expert_id="..."><quote>...</quote></source>`), and `<counterarguments>` (with `<counterargument>` elements)
- `<areas_of_agreement>` with `<area>` elements
- `<areas_of_disagreement>` with `<area>` elements
- `<uncertainties>` with `<uncertainty>` elements
- `<minority_reports>` with `<report expert_id="..." support_count="{n}">` elements, each containing `<position>`, `<evidence><quote>...</quote></evidence>`, and `<committee_assessment>`
- `<narrative>` with inline citation markers like [C1], [C2, C3]

Produce as many claims as the evidence supports. Do not artificially limit or pad the count. The number of claims should reflect the complexity and breadth of the expert input.
